Creating a named branch just to inspect an old commit is littering.
Every branch creates a file in '.git/refs/heads/' that persists until
someone remembers to delete it.

A detached HEAD points directly to a commit object rather than through
a named ref:
    HEAD -> 8a3f12c... (commit)
rather than:
    HEAD -> refs/heads/main -> 8a3f12c...

Worktrees support detached checkouts natively. You obtain an isolated
directory fixed to an exact revision without polluting the reference
namespace. When the review is complete, discard the directory.
